From dcba6195210a76fa3ec25b3c01a43b22feb13c4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bkool Classic contributor <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:45:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(serial): add Bkool Classic (USB) trainer adapter

Adds a serial adapter for the Bkool Trainer Classic, which can be
connected and controlled via its USB cable (FTDI serial, 115200 8N1).

- registered as serial protocol "Bkool Classic"
- check(): "$PC#" hello (reply "$RL<id>V<version>#") or console telemetry
- start(): sends total mass ($CW), wind ($CN0), rolling resistance ($CF4)
  and flat slope ($CS0)
- slope control in Smart Trainer mode via "$CS<slope % x 100>#"
  (negative values supported, clamped to +/-25 %, de-duplicated)
- power/speed taken from the trainer's console output ("SHOW" / "SPD")
- SerialInterface.openPort() accepts optional port props (baudRate)

The protocol was reverse engineered from the trainer (firmware V01.13);
it is not an official Bkool specification. Unit tests use MockBinding.
